PixelU-Wii patch for FatFs R0.14b, ffconf.h: the options PixelU-Wii's code
needs (Common/FatFsUtil.cpp builds and reads the SD card image,
Core/IOS/Network/KD/VFF/VFFUtil.cpp the WiiConnect24 VFF files).

  FF_USE_MKFS 1     f_mkfs(): a new SD card image is formatted.
  FF_USE_LFN 2      long file names, with the working buffer on the stack
                    (FatFsUtil.cpp supplies no ff_memalloc/ff_memfree).
  FF_LFN_UNICODE 2  file names on the API are UTF-8, as everywhere else in
                    PixelU-Wii.
  FF_FS_RPATH 1     f_chdir(): the SD image is filled from and copied to a
                    host folder one directory at a time.

Everything else stays at the R0.14b defaults.

--- a/source/ffconf.h
+++ b/source/ffconf.h
@@ -32,3 +32,3 @@
 
-#define FF_USE_MKFS		0
+#define FF_USE_MKFS		1
 /* This option switches f_mkfs() function. (0:Disable or 1:Enable) */
@@ -115,3 +115,3 @@
 
-#define FF_USE_LFN		0
+#define FF_USE_LFN		2
 #define FF_MAX_LFN		255
@@ -135,3 +135,3 @@
 
-#define FF_LFN_UNICODE	0
+#define FF_LFN_UNICODE	2
 /* This option switches the character encoding on the API when LFN is enabled.
@@ -155,3 +155,3 @@
 
-#define FF_FS_RPATH		0
+#define FF_FS_RPATH		1
 /* This option configures support for relative path.
